Prior ideation notes: ../../../backups/P095/P095.research-notes.md (21 searches, Armilla/AIUC/Corgi/etc.)
## Findings log
G1 (Seam Map) Risklytics = existing startup: AI platform analysing insurance policies, filings, AI liability gaps; tracks forms/endorsements/filings; founder Samuel Gold. https://datainnovation.org/2026/07/5-qs-with-samuel-gold-founder-of-risklytics/ (no funding data found). Fenwick already tells policyholders to do comprehensive policy reviews + DIC/captive/manuscript endorsements. No Marsh/Aon/WTW AI-exclusion tool found by search (negative; brokers do this bundled free). Bloomberg/Haynes Boone/Fenwick: renewal negotiation advice is free commentary.
G2 (Warranty File) Travelers v ICS: voluntarily dismissed 2022-08-26, policy stipulated rescinded after loss (insideprivacy/Reed Smith). Columbia Casualty v Cottage Health = negligent misrep argument. Verification startups exist: IntellectAI Risk Analyst (checks submissions vs outside signals), Coalition continuous scan, Cyberwrite, SecondSight/INSUREtrust Cyber Pre-Check. Marsh stat 41% of cyber apps denied on first submission (secondary, unverified). No incontestability endorsement for cyber found.
G3 (Mutual) Lawfare article (Trout, Kvist, Dattani) = ADVOCACY for frontier AI mutual "AIMIL" (Kvist is AIUC CEO; AIUC is therefore positioned to build it). No lab captive/mutual found. https://www.lawfaremedia.org/article/bootstrapping-frontier-ai-governance-by-mutualizing-risk . CrowdStrike Project QuiltWorks (May 28 2026) = insurers (Coalition, Liberty Mutual, Lockton, Resilience, Marsh) financing frontier AI cyber risk.
G1b Risklytics (SF) = AI platform that analyzes commercial policies + filings, finds AI-exclusion gaps, identifies carriers w/o exclusion or w/ affirmative AI cover, helps prepare governance docs; target = robotics/industrial automation/AI-enabled tech; partners w/ wholesale brokers + MGAs; funding/size/pricing undisclosed. https://datainnovation.org/2026/07/5-qs-with-samuel-gold-founder-of-risklytics/  => Seam Map core is already being built (small, early).
G3b Lawfare: mutual owned by frontier labs, member capital; claims "no new laws needed, first policies within 3 months"; no limits/premium/capital/members named; no copyright mention in fetched part. Authors Trout/Kvist/Dattani (Kvist believed AIUC CEO; fetch didn't state). 
G4 (Gate Meter) arXiv 2606.16465 "Trace-Economic Underwriting" + arXiv 2607.11999 "Underwriting the Agent Economy" (preprints on trace/telemetry-conditioned pricing); Mount (YC P26) building "AI-agent insurance carrier" with liability for deployed agents. No live gateway-telemetry-priced product found (confirms ideation negative) but academic/YC convergence => idea is obvious, not hidden.
G5 (Waive List) No Verisk AI exposure score found; Verisk GenAI Underwriting Assistant (Sept 2025) is property submission summarising. Unverified: >80% of exclusion filings approved (actuary.info). Berkley absolute exclusion.
G6 (Mirror) No CG 40 47 buy-back found (confirms ideation negative). DIC is a property concept; surplus lines DIC for liability is not standard.
G8 (Trigger) Parametrix already: parametric cloud-outage cover; monitoring extended to AI services (ChatGPT, Gemini, Claude) in 2024 (https://www.parametrixinsurance.com/in-the-news/parametrix-expands-monitoring-capabilities-to-ai-services-like-chatgpt); Cumulus Re cat bond (Hannover Re) upsized $20M->$35M (reinsurancene.ws), earlier deals expired untriggered. => cloud-outage cat bond market ~tens of $M, NOT $5B referenced limit. Munich Re aiSure parametric (single secondary src, EUR15M per claim). CSA note 2026-07-06 "Foundation Model Concentration: the uninsurable AI risk".
G6b Mount (YC P26, Fabian Amherd, John Bachmann): "AI-agent insurance carrier", Mount AI Liability Policy for mid-market/enterprise deploying agents; scans/red-teams, issues ADR certs ("SOC2 for agents"), uses eval data for pricing. Funding conflicting ($125k-$500k YC). https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/mount => seed-stage competitor for Gate Meter/Mirror/Warranty (telemetry+evidence -> underwriting).
G8b Cumulus Re (Hannover Re sponsor, Kaith Re issuer, Parametrix structuring+calc agent): 2024 $13.75M, 2025 $20M, 2026 $35M; none triggered; "14th cyber cat bond in Artemis directory, 3rd parametric". https://www.artemis.bm/deal-directory/cumulus-re-series-2026-1/ ; industry loss estimate Nov 2025 cloud disruption $5-15B. Parametrix Series B $27M Mundi (unconfirmed). Parametrix already = independent calc agent for cloud outage + AI service monitoring. => Trigger's "$5B referenced limit" is ~100x the whole existing cloud-outage ILS market.
G7 (Causation Desk) Appraisal case law: appraisal limited to amount of loss, NOT causation/coverage (CA, MN cases; propertyinsurancecoveragelaw.com) => "like appraisal" premise is legally wrong; panel finding would have to be contractual expert determination, enforceability varies; courts decide coverage questions. Litigation hold/AI log preservation is commentary-level; OpenAI NYT preservation order ended Sept 2025. No quantification of DJ action costs found.
G3c FT/Reuters: OpenAI up to $300M (one source says much lower), considered self-insure/captive; OpenAI says no captive now, evaluating structures. Aon's Kalinich: lacks capacity for model providers.
G3d AIUC: $40M Series A (Ribbit; First Harmonic, Terrain), reported 2026-09-17 fintech.global; total $55M; extending from agents to FRONTIER MODELS (audits, standards, insurance); CEO Rune Kvist (Anthropic's first product hire), co-founders Rajiv Dattani, Brandon Wang (CTO). The Lawfare frontier-AI-mutual authors = AIUC founders. https://fintech.global/2026/09/17/aiuc-raises-40m-to-police-risk-in-frontier-ai-agents/ => The Mutual's most likely builder is AIUC; it is also the pitch's natural competitor.  ElevenLabs announced AIUC-1-backed policy for voice agents (tracker July 2026, details undisclosed).
G8c Cyber cat bonds: ~$800M total risk transferred (Geneva Assoc., Dec 2024); largest single = Beazley PoleStar Re 2026-1 $300M. Whole cat-bond market $65.5B outstanding (Artemis Q3 2026). => Trigger's $5B referenced limit > entire cyber ILS market. https://www.genevaassociation.org/sites/default/files/2026-08/cyber_ils_summary_120826.pdf
G5b Waive List: no source that reinsurance treaties require blanket attachment (negative; Evercore forecast only). Gallagher cyber leader: "a few carriers starting to adopt" exclusions (Insurance Business "Insurers, brokers adjust as AI exclusions emerge") vs 60+ groups filed ISO forms => actual attach rate uncertain; some carriers sell coverage back onto CGL for added premium once they understand AI use/guardrails (unnamed, unpriced; Insurance Business). HSB (Munich Re) standalone AI liability for SMBs launched Mar 2026.
G4b No gateway-vendor<->insurer partnership found (Cloudflare/Portkey/LiteLLM/Kong). Armilla partner program (Trustible = AI governance platform). 
